# Web Page Copy — Pixel-Perfect Website Capture to Figma

Captures any live external website pixel-perfectly into Figma — exact logo, nav, hero, typography, spacing, images, gradients, icons, and separators. Then optionally overlays new design components (e.g. author bios, CTAs, banners) at precise positions within the captured page.

## When to use
- "Copy this page exactly into Figma"
- "Recreate this website pixel-for-pixel"
- "Capture [URL] and add [component] to it"
- Any time you need a pixel-accurate Figma representation of a live page to present a design addition or change in full context

## What makes this work
Playwright strips Content Security Policy headers from all responses, injects the Figma capture script into the live DOM, scrolls to load lazy images, then submits the full rendered page to Figma. The result is the actual rendered page — not a screenshot — including real fonts, real colors, real spacing, real SVGs and images.

## Required setup
- Playwright installed: `cd /tmp && mkdir pw-capture && cd pw-capture && npm init -y && npm install playwright && npx playwright install chromium`
- Figma MCP authenticated (plugin:figma:figma tools available)
- Target Figma file exists (create with `create_new_file` if needed)

