## Step-by-step process

### Step 1 — Get capture IDs (one per page)
Call `generate_figma_design` once per page you want to capture. Each call returns a single-use `captureId`. Get ALL capture IDs upfront before running any Playwright scripts.

```
generate_figma_design({ fileKey: "YOUR_FILE_KEY" })
// Returns: captureId: "xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx"
```

For N pages, call N times in parallel to get N capture IDs.

### Step 2 — Run Playwright capture (one per page, run in parallel/background)

```javascript
// capture-page.js
const { chromium } = require('playwright');

(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true });
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  const page = await context.newPage();
  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 1440, height: 900 });

  // CRITICAL: Strip CSP headers so the capture script can inject
  await page.route('**/*', async (route) => {
    const response = await route.fetch();
    const headers = { ...response.headers() };
    delete headers['content-security-policy'];
    delete headers['content-security-policy-report-only'];
    await route.fulfill({ response, headers });
  });

  await page.goto('TARGET_URL', { waitUntil: 'networkidle', timeout: 45000 });

  // Dismiss cookie banners
  try { await page.click('button:has-text("Ok, got it")', { timeout: 3000 }); await page.waitForTimeout(500); } catch {}
  try { await page.click('button:has-text("Accept")', { timeout: 1000 }); } catch {}

  // Scroll to load ALL lazy images
  await page.evaluate(async () => {
    await new Promise(resolve => {
      let total = 0;
      const timer = setInterval(() => {
        window.scrollBy(0, 400);
        total += 400;
        if (total > document.body.scrollHeight) { clearInterval(timer); resolve(); }
      }, 100);
    });
  });
  await page.evaluate(() => window.scrollTo(0, 0));
  await page.waitForTimeout(1500);

  // Inject Figma capture script
  const captureScriptRes = await page.context().request.get('https://mcp.figma.com/mcp/html-to-design/capture.js');
  const captureScript = await captureScriptRes.text();
  await page.evaluate((s) => {
    const el = document.createElement('script');
    el.textContent = s;
    document.head.appendChild(el);
  }, captureScript);
  await page.waitForTimeout(800);

  // Submit capture
  const result = await page.evaluate(() =>
    window.figma.captureForDesign({
      captureId: 'CAPTURE_ID_FROM_STEP_1',
      endpoint: 'https://mcp.figma.com/mcp/capture/CAPTURE_ID_FROM_STEP_1/submit',
      selector: 'body'
    })
  );

  console.log('Done:', JSON.stringify(result));
  await browser.close();
})();
```

Run with: `node capture-page.js`
For multiple pages simultaneously: use `run_in_background: true` on the Bash tool.

### Step 3 — Poll until completed

```
generate_figma_design({ fileKey: "YOUR_FILE_KEY", captureId: "CAPTURE_ID" })
```

- Status `pending` or `processing` → wait 5 seconds, poll again
- Status `completed` → returns node ID of the captured frame in Figma
- Poll up to 10 times before troubleshooting

### Step 4 — Add design components to the capture (optional)

After capture completes, the page is a real Figma frame. To add overlaid components (bio cards, banners, CTAs, annotations):

**CRITICAL: Captured pages have nested auto-layout containers. Appending children to auto-layout frames collapses them to 0 height. Always add overlay components as direct children of the ROOT CAPTURE FRAME (layout mode = NONE), not inner containers.**

```javascript
// use_figma: Add component as absolute overlay on capture
const captureFrame = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync("CAPTURE_NODE_ID");
// captureFrame.layoutMode will be "NONE" — safe to add absolute children

const component = figma.createFrame();
component.x = 0;
component.y = TARGET_Y; // position within the capture
component.resize(1440, HEIGHT);
// ... build component ...
captureFrame.appendChild(component); // Direct child = absolute positioning
```

**Finding target Y position:**
```javascript
// Find a reference node and get its absolute canvas Y
function absolutePos(node) {
  let x = 0, y = 0, n = node;
  while (n && n.type !== 'PAGE') { x += n.x||0; y += n.y||0; n = n.parent; }
  return { x: Math.round(x), y: Math.round(y) };
}
const refNode = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync("NODE_ID");
const refAbs = absolutePos(refNode);
const captureAbs = absolutePos(captureFrame);
const relY = refAbs.y - captureAbs.y; // Y relative to capture frame
```

