## Common gotchas

| Problem | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Capture submits but page looks broken | CSP blocked script injection | Route handler must delete BOTH csp headers before `page.goto` |
| Lazy images missing | Page not scrolled before capture | Always scroll to bottom then back to top before injecting script |
| Component collapses to 0 height after append | Appended to auto-layout child frame | Append to ROOT capture frame (layoutMode: NONE) instead |
| captureId not found | Used wrong captureId in Playwright script | Each page needs its own unique captureId — never reuse |
| Capture stays "pending" forever | Script injection failed silently | Check CSP stripping; verify `window.figma` is defined after injection |
| Cookie banner blocks content | Banner not dismissed | Try multiple button text variants: "Ok, got it", "Accept", "Accept All" |

---

## Key insight (why this works vs screenshots)
Regular screenshots give a PNG — no layers, no text, no real assets. The Figma capture script converts the live rendered DOM into actual Figma frames with real fills, real text nodes, real image hashes, and real layout. The result is editable, zoomable, and accurate to the pixel because it reads the browser's computed styles directly.
